# Bluetooth PAN: IpClient in the Bluetooth process asks for netd's binder service and logs
# "returning null INetd instance". AOSP forbids it (neverallow, netd.te). DHCP does not need it:
# IpClient sets the IPv4 address through NetworkManagementService; netd is only for static
# addresses (InterfaceController.addAddress).
dontaudit bluetooth netd_service:service_manager find;
